Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Intersection numbers of divisors from a triangulated GTP", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"38ca571d-8f20-4439-9b1a-a4e714981d6c"],

Cell["\<\
This is a companion code for the paper \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]5d SCFTs and \
Intersection Theory for Generalized Toric Threefolds\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] \
by Arguz, Bourget, Bousseau, Grimminger, Schafer-Nameki, 2026. 

It implements the algorithm described in Section 6. The input is a fully \
triangulated GTP / Symington polygon, with 7-branes pulled in. It outputs the \
intersection numbers of a basis of divisors. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.00218428086007*^9, 4.002184288650836*^9}, {
  4.002184641341134*^9, 
  4.002184768456469*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"5d445ad1-0263-49cf-b2f5-\
cf7c97d295d9"],

Cell["\<\
Conventions.  
(o) Notations follow the paper as much as possible. 
(i) The generalized face (T-cone) swept out when the 7-brane is pulled in is \
NOT triangulated: it is removed from the polygon and its two sides -- the cut \
and its monodromy image -- are glued.  So the interior edges of the face must \
not appear in the edge list, while the two sides of the cut must.  
(ii) A brane is given as {charge, cut}, where cut = {v, ...} starts at the \
tip v of the wedge; the other side of the wedge is cutImage[{charge,cut}].  \
The convention is that the polygon lies counterclockwise from the cut, which \
fixes the sign of the monodromy-invariant direction u of the E-line.  A third \
element may be supplied, {charge, cut, u}, to override that choice.  
(iii) Divisors are numbered by the order in which the vertices first appear \
in the edge list, and the compact double curves by the order of their edges, \
so the edge list can be ordered to match a desired labelling.  
(iv) The charge {p,q} is the [p,q] of the draft, whose matrix M_[p,q] acts on \
charges.  Its transpose acts on directions in the polygon and maps the side \
cutImage[{charge,cut}] of the wedge onto the cut
(v) The E-line \[ScriptL]_\[Alpha] is followed through the triangulation and \
across the cuts.  At a compact vertex that it meets, the deformed line passes \
on its left, or on its right when the tip of another 7-brane lies on the left \
next to that vertex (the option \"BypassSide\" -> \"Left\" or \"Right\" \
forces a side), and crosses the edges of the star of that vertex on that \
side.  The choice should not matter.  \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0021848240077763`*^9, 4.002184928634344*^9}, {
  4.0021856346004267`*^9, 
  4.00218563773706*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"f0205cf8-f0a3-4c53-943c-\
8093e86be7d0"],

Cell["\<\
Main entry points.
  gtpRun[]                         \t\t\t\tdraw a GTP and do everything: \
picture, computation, intersection numbers, TikZ code.
  gtpRun[edges, branes]           \t\t          the same for a given GTP, \
without the editor.
  gtpReport[res]                                                 prints the \
dictionaries, the \[Alpha] and \[Beta] tables and the intersection matrices.
  gtpIntersectionTables[res]     \t         just the matrices D_i.D_j.D_k.
  gtpPlot[res]                \t\t\t         the picture of the GTP.
  gtpTikZ[res]                 \t\t\t        the same picture as LaTeX/TikZ \
source.
  gtpConsistencyChecks[res]                      geometric tests of the \
output.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002184985163414*^9, 
  4.002185051771717*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"638eca27-627c-4258-a8f9-\
5e3ca44bcdc0"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Load the package", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"0deae9fd-e049-42d2-86bf-cf6109ee8b41"],

Cell["\<\
Evaluate this initialization cell first: it loads GTPIntersections.wl from \
the folder of this notebook.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ab21f169-9bca-4f4e-9c9a-3e426ecd67d5"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Get", "[", 
  RowBox[{"FileNameJoin", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"NotebookDirectory", "[", "]"}], ",", " ", 
     "\"\<GTPIntersections.wl\>\""}], "}"}], "]"}], "]"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->True,
 CellLabel->"In[2]:=",ExpressionUUID->"d96d1fcc-1df6-41fb-bee1-0f9c15143281"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Draw a GTP and compute everything", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1f004e3f-2fe8-4193-9b20-fe8276994697"],

Cell["\<\
gtpRun[] asks for the size of the grid and opens the editor: draw the edges \
of the triangulation and the 7-brane cuts, then click Done.  
It prints the input (as a command gtpRun[edges, branes] that redoes the \
computation without the editor), the picture of the GTP, the computation, the \
triple intersection numbers and the TikZ code of the picture, with buttons \
that copy it.  
Options: \"Report\" -> False (picture, intersection numbers and TikZ code \
only), \"TikZFile\" -> \"fig.tex\" (also write the TikZ code to that file, \
next to this notebook), \"TikZOptions\" -> {...} and \"PlotOptions\" -> {...} \
(options of gtpTikZ and gtpPlot).\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.002185667456111*^9, 
  4.002185674135689*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"6c91ec5a-9caa-423f-9b13-\
3210f945dd17"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"res", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"gtpRun", "[", "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 CellLabel->"In[24]:=",ExpressionUUID->"c2360348-2933-449d-82b6-90cf1db57c13"],

Cell["To modify the GTP just computed, reopen it in the editor:", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7cfdba69-232f-4cad-8601-5570e34ce1ee"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"res", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"gtpRun", "[", 
    RowBox[{"5", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"Sequence", " ", "@@", " ", 
      RowBox[{"res", "[", "\"\<Input\>\"", "]"}]}]}], "]"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",\

 CellLabel->"In[4]:=",ExpressionUUID->"edb8945a-9ef8-4631-8821-28e1f0b5b497"]
}, Open  ]],

